From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:05:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Input: s6sy761 - resume asynchronously

Powering the SPI controller up and polling for its boot-complete event
takes about 190 ms on a Pixel 6 Pro. Resumed in order, that held up the
whole system resume, and with it the display and the key press that
woke the phone. Let it resume asynchronously; its SPI controller, the
parent, still resumes first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c
index 9db081d56..22136f9e6 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/s6sy761.c
@@ -821,6 +821,13 @@ static int s6sy761_probe_common(struct s6sy761_data *sdata)
 
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * Powering the SPI controller up and waiting for its boot event takes
+	 * some 200 ms; done in order it holds up the whole system resume, the
+	 * display and the key that woke the phone with it.
+	 */
+	device_enable_async_suspend(dev);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
